                <pb facs="0388" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg308"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hart to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hart inquires if he is to understand, from Department’s instruction No. 407,
                    of June 28, 1902, that due compensation must be made at the time of seizure of
                    property; and states that American citizens must continue to suffer without
                    practical remedy if such rule is not observed.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
